      "reason": "BitOp and its four variants moved from kevy-embedded to kevy-store, where the byte arithmetic they name now lives so both surfaces can call one implementation. kevy-embedded/without-example fell 170 -> 165 by exactly those items; kevy-store/without-example rose 285 -> 289, four rather than five because the enum itself gained an executable example. The deficit is one item smaller overall; the ratchet is keyed per crate, so a move between crates shows as growth in the receiving key. bitop_combine and Route::BitOpStore both carry examples that teach \u2014 the padding rules and the 0xff tail of NOT, and why BITOP cannot ride Route::Single(1).",
